[Glimt Decoder]
Name=GIMP (ImageMagick)
Comment=GIMP's own files, their visible layers put together, through ImageMagick
Extensions=xcf
# GIMP keeps no composite: the layers are merged here, transparency kept (PAM). ImageMagick
# reads XCF of GIMP 2.8 and older fully; for newer files, export from GIMP if a layer is missing.
# The format is named before the path ("xcf:"): without it ImageMagick goes by what the bytes
# say, and a file from the internet named .xcf could reach Ghostscript or another coder.
Exec=convert xcf:%f -background none -layers merge -depth 8 pam:-
